# Each case: which agent answers which message, and which checks the answer must pass.
#
# agent:   an agent class in this app. It is built with `message:`, `provider:` and `model:` (see Evaluation::Case#build_agent
#          if yours needs more, such as a record or a user).
# checks:  names of `check_*` methods in Evaluation::Checks. A hash passes parameters:
#            - finished                          # the model finished: not cut off, not refused
#            - structured                        # the agent's response_schema produced an object
#            - { max_seconds: { seconds: 20 } }
#            - { max_output_tokens: { tokens: 500 } }
#            - { contains: { text: "refund" } }  # also: excludes, matches
#
# The agent's own `max_tokens` applies, so compare at the limits you will ship: a cap that suits one provider can truncate
# another (the "cut off" row of the scorecard).
#
# Use real scenarios. A good set mixes ordinary cases, awkward ones, and the failures you would hate to ship.

- id: smoke_test
  title: The agent answers and finishes
  agent: ApplicationAgent
  message: "Reply with exactly one word: ok"
  checks:
    - finished
    - { max_seconds: { seconds: 30 } }
    - { contains: { text: "ok" } }
